# Next.js App Router Installation Guide

## 1. Package Installation
```bash
npm install better-auth
```

## 2. Environment Variables
Create a `.env` file with:
```
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=<your-32-char-secret>
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<your-google-id>
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<your-google-secret>
```

Generate a secret using `openssl rand -base64 32`.

## 3. Server Auth Configuration
Create `lib/auth.ts`:
```ts
import { betterAuth } from "better-auth";
import Database from "better-sqlite3";

export const auth = betterAuth({
  database: new Database("./sqlite.db"),
  emailAndPassword: { enabled: true },
  socialProviders: {
    google: {
      clientId: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID!,
      clientSecret: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET!,
    },
  },
});
```

## 4. Client Setup
Create `lib/auth-client.ts`:
```ts
import { createAuthClient } from "better-auth/react";

export const authClient = createAuthClient({
  baseURL: "http://localhost:3000"
});
```

## 5. API Route Handler
Create `app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts`:
```ts
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth";
import { toNextJsHandler } from "better-auth/next-js";

export const { POST, GET } = toNextJsHandler(auth);
```

## 6. Database Schema
Run the migration command:
```bash
npx auth@latest migrate
```

Or use `npx auth@latest generate` to create migration files manually.

## 7. Server-Side Session
Access the current session using `auth.api.getSession(request)` in server components or API routes with the request object.

